## 1. Architecture (ADR-000 / ADR-001)

Clean Architecture + CQRS via MediatR. Multi-tenant clinic management system.

```
TenantCore.Api ──► TenantCore.Application ──► TenantCore.Domain
TenantCore.Api ──► TenantCore.Infrastructure ──► TenantCore.Domain
TenantCore.Web.Client ──► TenantCore.Shared
All layers ──► TenantCore.Shared (DTOs / constants only)
```

**Rule:** inner layers NEVER reference outer layers. Domain references nothing.

| Project | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `TenantCore.Api` | Entry / composition root — thin controllers, middleware, JWT, DI wiring, Swagger, Serilog |
| `TenantCore.Application` | CQRS — commands, queries, handlers, validators, translators, pipeline behaviors, service interfaces |
| `TenantCore.Domain` | Entities (`BaseEntity` / `AuditableEntity`), repository interfaces, domain exceptions — zero deps |
| `TenantCore.Infrastructure` | EF Core `ClinicDbContext`, `ClinicRepository<T>` + repositories, Fluent configs, external services, Auth HTTP client |
| `TenantCore.Shared` | DTOs, `AuthorizationConstants`, enums, `Result<T>` / `PagedResult<T>` — zero deps |
| `TenantCore.Web.Client` | Blazor WASM — typed HTTP clients, pages, components (HTTP-only, no server refs) |
| `TenantCore.Web` | Blazor server host |
| `TenantCore.Logging` | Centralized logging to Azure Table Storage (`ApiErrorLogs`, `FrontendErrorLogs`, `ActionLogs`) |
| `Requirements` | Requirements documents |

**Test projects:** `tests/TenantCore.Api.Tests`, `TenantCore.Application.Tests`, `TenantCore.Domain.Tests`, `TenantCore.Infrastructure.Tests`, `TenantCore.Web.Client.Tests`.
**Tools:** `tools/MedicineNormalizer`.

---

## 2. Coding patterns (quick reference)

### Controller — `src/TenantCore.Api/Controllers/`
Thin. Clinic-scoped controllers inherit `ClinicControllerBase`. Only `ISender` injected. Zero business logic.

```csharp
[ApiController]
[Route("api/[controller]")]
[Produces("application/json")]
public class PatientsController(ISender sender) : ClinicControllerBase(sender)
{
    [HttpGet]
    [ProducesResponseType(typeof(IEnumerable<PatientSummaryDto>), StatusCodes.Status200OK)]
    public async Task<IActionResult> GetAll(CancellationToken ct)
        => Ok(await sender.Send(new GetPatientsQuery(GetApplicationId()), ct));

    [HttpPost]
    [ProducesResponseType(typeof(Guid), StatusCodes.Status201Created)]
    public async Task<IActionResult> Create([FromBody] CreatePatientRequest request, CancellationToken ct)
    {
        var id = await sender.Send(new CreatePatientCommand(request, GetApplicationId()), ct);
        return CreatedAtAction(nameof(GetById), new { id }, id);
    }
}
```
- Use `GetApplicationId()` from the base class — never read the `X-Application-Id` header directly.
- Always pass `ApplicationId` into commands and queries.

### Command / Query — `Features/{Area}/Commands|Queries/`
`sealed record` implementing `IRequest<T>` (delete/void → `IRequest`).

```csharp
public sealed record CreatePatientCommand(CreatePatientRequest Request, Guid ApplicationId) : IRequest<Guid>;
public sealed record DeletePatientCommand(Guid Id, Guid ApplicationId) : IRequest;
public sealed record GetPatientsQuery(Guid ApplicationId) : IRequest<IEnumerable<PatientSummaryDto>>;
```

### Handler — `Features/{Area}/Handlers/`
`sealed class`, primary constructor, one handler per command/query file.

```csharp
public sealed class CreatePatientHandler(IPatientRepository repository, ILogger<CreatePatientHandler> logger)
    : IRequestHandler<CreatePatientCommand, Guid>
{ /* map via translator, AddAsync, SaveChangesAsync, return Id */ }
```
- Throw `EntityNotFoundException` on not-found — never return null or error DTOs.
- Generate IDs in the translator, not in the handler.

### Validator — `Features/{Area}/Validators/`
`AbstractValidator<T>` (FluentValidation), auto-registered by assembly scan. Every string: `NotEmpty()` + `MaximumLength(N)`. Validate `Guid.Empty` for IDs; `Enum.IsDefined` before enum use.

### Translator — `Features/{Area}/Translators/`
`static class` with `static` methods (`ToEntity`, `ToDto`, `ToSummaryDto`). **Never AutoMapper.**

### Repository interface — `src/TenantCore.Domain/Interfaces/`
Extends `IRepository<T>` (generic base: `GetByIdAsync`, `GetAllAsync`, `AddAsync`, `Update`, `Delete`, `ExistsAsync`, `SaveChangesAsync`). Add only extra queries; always accept `Guid applicationId`.

### Repository implementation — `src/TenantCore.Infrastructure/Repositories/`
Inherit `ClinicRepository<T>`; always filter by `applicationId`; `AsNoTracking()` on reads.

### EF config — `src/TenantCore.Infrastructure/Persistence/Configurations/`
`IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>`, Fluent API only (no Data Annotations on entities), configure `RowVersion` as row version.

### DTOs — `src/TenantCore.Shared/Dtos/`
`record` with `init` setters. Detail `XDto`, list `XSummaryDto`, input `CreateXRequest` / `UpdateXRequest`. No methods, no validation attributes, no business logic.

### DI + migrations
- Application DI: `AddApplication()` · Infrastructure DI: `AddInfrastructure()`. Handlers/validators auto-scan. New repository → register `Scoped` in Infrastructure DI.
- Migrations:
```bash
dotnet ef migrations add <Name> --project src/TenantCore.Infrastructure --startup-project src/TenantCore.Api --output-dir Persistence/ClinicMigrations
dotnet ef database update --project src/TenantCore.Infrastructure --startup-project src/TenantCore.Api
```

---

## 3. Hard rules (never violate — from CLAUDE.md)

- Controllers inherit `ClinicControllerBase` and only call `sender.Send(...)` — no service injection.
- Commands and queries are `sealed record`; handlers are `sealed class`.
- Translators are `static class` with `static` methods — never AutoMapper.
- No business logic in controllers, repositories, or middleware.
- No EF Core in Application or Domain layers.
- No Data Annotations on Domain entities — use Fluent API configurations.
- Always include `ApplicationId` on tenant-scoped commands/queries.
- Always filter by `applicationId` in tenant-scoped repository queries.
- Throw exceptions for errors; never return error DTOs from handlers.
- Do not change the middleware pipeline order (ADR-005).
- Every feature must ship with unit tests (ADR-009).
- Every delete/remove/clear action must confirm first via the shared `ConfirmDialog` component (ADR-007).

### Error handling
Throw domain exceptions — `ExceptionHandlingMiddleware` converts to ProblemDetails.

| Exception | HTTP status |
|---|---|
| `ValidationException` (FluentValidation via pipeline) | 400 |
| `EntityNotFoundException` | 404 |
| `InvalidOperationException` | 409 |
| `UnauthorizedAccessException` | 401 |

Never return error responses manually from handlers or controllers.

### Authorization
`[Authorize(Policy = AuthPolicies.RequireAuthenticated | RequireClinicAdmin | RequireReception | RequireClinical)]`.
Constants live in `TenantCore.Shared/Authorization/AuthorizationConstants.cs` — never use raw string literals.

---

## 4. Multi-tenancy (ADR-008) — critical

```
X-Application-Id header
  → ClinicContextMiddleware (validates against the JWT "app_ids" claim; 403 if absent/not owned)
  → HttpContext.Items["ApplicationId"]
  → ClinicControllerBase.GetApplicationId()
  → command/query ApplicationId field
  → repository WHERE ApplicationId = @applicationId
```
- Never read the `X-Application-Id` header in a controller.
- Never accept `ApplicationId` from `[FromBody]` — only from `GetApplicationId()`.
- Every tenant-scoped entity has `public Guid ApplicationId { get; set; }`.
- Test: "can two different clinics have different values/records for this?" → yes ⇒ tenant-scoped.
- Global reference/lookup data (e.g. `MedicineDosageForm`, `DoctorSpeciality`) is **not** tenant-scoped.

---

## 5. Testing (ADR-009) — mandatory for every feature

Stack: xUnit 2.4.2, Moq, FluentAssertions, `Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk`. Test folders mirror `Features/{Area}/...`.
Naming: `MethodName_Scenario_ExpectedResult` (e.g. `Handle_PatientNotFound_ThrowsEntityNotFoundException`).

Per-feature required coverage:
- **Handlers** — happy path (`AddAsync` + `SaveChangesAsync` called, correct data captured), `ApplicationId` set on entity, all fields mapped, `EntityNotFoundException` on not-found, cross-tenant entity treated as not-found, empty list returns empty (not exception).
- **Validators** — fully valid passes; each required field fails on null/empty (`[Theory]` + `[InlineData]`); `MaximumLength` boundary (over fails, at passes); empty `ApplicationId` fails.
- **Translators** — `ToEntity` maps all properties + generates non-empty `Id` + sets `ApplicationId`; `ToDto` / `ToSummaryDto` map all fields.

Do **NOT** test EF Core internals, DTO setters, or `Program.cs` wiring.

```bash
dotnet test
dotnet test tests/TenantCore.Application.Tests/
```

---

## 6. Security & code quality (ADR-010)

**Checklist:** every controller/action has explicit `[Authorize(...)]` or `[AllowAnonymous]` (with a comment); destructive ops ≥ `RequireClinicAdmin`; string inputs `NotEmpty()` + `MaximumLength()`; route IDs typed `Guid`; enums checked with `Enum.IsDefined`; `pageSize` capped (≤100); no `ExecuteSqlRaw` with user input; `AsNoTracking()` on read queries; no `IQueryable<T>` returned from repositories; no secrets/passwords in logs; errors flow through middleware; CorrelationId forwarded on AuthApi calls.

**Code smells (S1–S12) & architectural violations (V1–V7) to detect:** wrong dependency direction (Application→Infrastructure, Domain→anything), controller not inheriting `ClinicControllerBase`, feature files outside `Features/`, non-`record` commands/queries, repository exposing `DbContext`, duplicate repository methods, generic `catch (Exception)`, handler returning null instead of throwing.

**Safe-fix rules (ADR-010 §11):** read the file first; find all callers before changing a signature; preserve observable behavior; one logical fix per edit; do not refactor surrounding code.
**Never change without explicit user instruction:** migration files, `RowVersion` concurrency config, middleware pipeline order, JWT validation parameters, `GetApplicationId()` implementation.

**Blazor client specifics (ADR-007):** no MudBlazor (removed — use native HTML with `opd-*`, `form-*`, `cc-*` classes); use `DateTimeHelper.ToLocalString()` for UTC-stored dates; `DateTime.Today` for "today" on the client; send `utcOffset` for UTC date-range filters; confirm before destructive actions; print pages open via `window.open` and use a red "✕ Close" button.

