## 7. Workflow — 3 phases (mirrors `.claude/commands`, read-only)

Claude's canonical command definitions live in `.claude/commands/`. I mirror their discipline; I never modify them.

**Phase 1 — Plan** (mirrors `plan-app-feature.md`)
1. Read `.claude/context/current-state.md` and `plan/REGISTRY.md`; verify the DbSet count matches the actual `ClinicDbContext.cs`.
2. Read `CLAUDE.md` + `docs/adr/ADR-000-index.md`, then only the ADRs relevant to the layers touched.
3. Present a **pre-plan brief** — domain area, layers affected, tenant-scoped?, EF migration?, files to create/modify, key decisions/open questions — and **wait for explicit approval**.
4. On approval, write `plan/<feature-name>/PLAN.md` (Overview, entity property table, Files to Create, Files to Modify, API Endpoints, Validation Rules, Business Rules, Multi-Tenancy Checklist, EF migration, Implementation Order, Test Files to Create).

**Phase 2 — Execute** (mirrors `execute-app-feature.md`)
Implement in PLAN.md order: Shared DTOs → Domain entity → repo interface → EF config → repo impl → `ClinicDbContext` (+DbSet) → Infrastructure DI (register) → Application commands/queries → validators → translator → handlers → API controller → unit tests → **migration reminder (print the command; do NOT auto-run)**.
Then: verify the multi-tenancy checklist; run `dotnet test tests/TenantCore.Application.Tests/` and confirm green; update `.claude/context/current-state.md` and `plan/REGISTRY.md`; print a completion table; suggest the security phase next.

**Phase 3 — Security** (mirrors `security-app-feature.md`)
Scan the implementation against ADR-010; report findings by severity with file/line + proposed fix; **ask which to fix** (`fix all` / `fix critical` / `fix security` / `fix quality` / `fix [IDs]` / `skip`); apply approved fixes per §11 safe-fix rules; write `plan/<feature>/SECURITY.md`.

---

## 8. Configuration layering (ADR-005)

`Program.cs` load order — later wins: `appsettings.json` → `appsettings.{Environment}.json` → **`appsettings.Local.json`** (last, gitignored).
- `appsettings.json` / `appsettings.Development.json`: **placeholders only** — checked in, never real secrets or working connection strings.
- `appsettings.Local.json`: the **real local values**.

New config key ⇒ add it to **both** files (placeholder + real value).

---

## 9. New-feature file layout (`Foo`)

```
src/TenantCore.Shared/Dtos/                                  FooDto.cs, CreateFooRequest.cs, UpdateFooRequest.cs
src/TenantCore.Domain/Entities/                              Foo.cs
src/TenantCore.Domain/Interfaces/                            IFooRepository.cs
src/TenantCore.Infrastructure/Persistence/Configurations/    FooConfiguration.cs
src/TenantCore.Infrastructure/Repositories/                  FooRepository.cs
src/TenantCore.Infrastructure/Persistence/ClinicDbContext.cs        (modify: +DbSet<Foo>)
src/TenantCore.Infrastructure/DependencyInjection.cs               (modify: register IFooRepository)
src/TenantCore.Application/Features/Foos/{Commands,Queries,Handlers,Validators,Translators}/
src/TenantCore.Api/Controllers/                              FoosController.cs
tests/TenantCore.Application.Tests/Features/Foos/{Commands,Queries,Validators,Translators}/
```
Namespaces/types follow: commands `CreateFooCommand` (`sealed record`), handlers `CreateFooHandler` (`sealed class`), validators `CreateFooCommandValidator` (`AbstractValidator<T>`), translators `FooTranslator` (`static`).

